WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.760
I'm Jenna Fisher.

2
00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:06.080
And I'm Angela Kinsey.

3
00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:07.360
We were on The Office together.

4
00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:08.600
And we're best friends.

5
00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:12.420
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.

6
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:19.420
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.

7
00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:20.560
We're The Office ladies.

8
00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:26.350
Angela just turned out the lights in the studio.

9
00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:27.850
Okay, here's the thing.

10
00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:29.310
There's a lot of buttons.

11
00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:31.590
This is what I want from a light switch.

12
00:00:31.850 --> 00:00:33.010
I want one button.

13
00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:35.130
There's four buttons over there, Jenna.

14
00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:35.690
There's more than four.

15
00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:37.630
You guys, it is a complicated light switch.

16
00:00:37.810 --> 00:00:38.210
Thank you.

17
00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:41.010
But we like to listen to our theme song to get in the mood.

18
00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:42.990
So we're listening to it with you.

19
00:00:43.490 --> 00:00:46.590
All during our theme song, Angela is pressing the buttons.

20
00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:47.690
The lights are going up.

21
00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:48.430
They're going down.

22
00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:49.350
They're fading in.

23
00:00:49.510 --> 00:00:50.550
There's track lighting.

24
00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:52.210
Then there's these other kind of lights.

25
00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:53.090
Ceiling lights.

26
00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:55.050
Then there's four lamps.

27
00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:56.970
We should turn some of the lamps on.

28
00:00:57.110 --> 00:00:57.830
That might help me.

29
00:00:57.930 --> 00:01:00.250
We need the light because our eyes are fading.

30
00:01:00.630 --> 00:01:02.910
Because I can't see, guys.

31
00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:03.870
That's what's happening.

32
00:01:04.050 --> 00:01:05.090
But all right, we're here.

33
00:01:05.090 --> 00:01:06.290
The lights are on.

34
00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:07.230
And we are ready.

35
00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:15.450
We are ready for Lecture Circuit Part 1, Season 5, Episode 16, written by Mindy Kaling and

36
00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:17.190
directed by Ken Kwapis.

37
00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:19.110
It's an official two-parter.

38
00:01:19.330 --> 00:01:20.230
It is.

39
00:01:20.230 --> 00:01:21.930
And I've got a whole fast fact about it.

40
00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:23.990
Oh, look how your face just lit up.

41
00:01:24.170 --> 00:01:25.530
You're so excited.

42
00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:26.510
I am.

43
00:01:26.770 --> 00:01:28.370
Here is your summary.

44
00:01:28.370 --> 00:01:37.090
Michael, accompanied by Pam, is embarking on a three-day lecture tour of the nearby Dunder Mifflin branches.

45
00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:38.590
I need to stop you one second.

46
00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:38.870
Yeah.

47
00:01:39.290 --> 00:01:40.090
Three days.

48
00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:40.710
Yeah.

49
00:01:40.990 --> 00:01:44.210
Three days Pam is going to be on the road with Michael.

50
00:01:44.430 --> 00:01:46.030
And she's so cheery about it.

51
00:01:46.110 --> 00:01:46.910
At the beginning.

52
00:01:48.770 --> 00:01:53.510
Well, you know, Michael's branch is outselling all the other branches.

53
00:01:53.790 --> 00:01:55.750
David Wallace is perplexed.

54
00:01:55.890 --> 00:01:57.250
What's that secret sauce?

55
00:01:57.650 --> 00:02:00.710
Please go to the other branches and tell them all about it.

56
00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:00.890
Yeah.

57
00:02:01.210 --> 00:02:02.870
Well, they're going to start in Utica.

58
00:02:03.110 --> 00:02:07.890
This is where they're going to run into Karen, and they are met with a surprise.

59
00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:08.370
Yeah.

60
00:02:09.050 --> 00:02:16.470
But back in Scranton, we reveal that Jim and Dwight are now the co-heads of the party planning committee.

61
00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:20.590
And they forgot Kelly's birthday.

62
00:02:20.890 --> 00:02:22.730
And she is ticked off.

63
00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:24.810
Oh, that is an understatement.

64
00:02:25.730 --> 00:02:30.670
Meanwhile, Andy has a crush on one of Stanley's clients.

65
00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:32.330
Fast fact number one.

66
00:02:32.490 --> 00:02:32.890
Mm-hmm.

67
00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:35.790
Lecture Circuit is a two-part episode.

68
00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:45.210
It aired two different weeks, and this is our first episode to ever feature a to-be-continued message, you know, at the end of the episode.

69
00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:48.850
But Lecture Circuit was not written as two episodes.

70
00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:53.710
It was one script, like your regular 41 pages long.

71
00:02:54.070 --> 00:02:55.870
We shot it in five days.

72
00:02:56.050 --> 00:02:57.930
So why did they make it a two-parter, Jenna?

73
00:02:58.270 --> 00:02:59.110
I will tell you.

74
00:02:59.190 --> 00:03:00.130
I thought you might.

75
00:03:00.350 --> 00:03:03.370
I was trading emails with director Ken Kwapis.

76
00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:08.630
He told me that when they went to assemble it in the editing room, there was so much good stuff.

77
00:03:08.630 --> 00:03:11.230
His director's cut was 35 minutes long.

78
00:03:11.570 --> 00:03:15.230
He showed it to Greg, and he said, Greg, I can't cut anymore.

79
00:03:15.510 --> 00:03:16.050
That's it.

80
00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:17.550
It's got to be 35 minutes, Greg.

81
00:03:17.870 --> 00:03:19.270
Yeah, make it supersized.

82
00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:19.470
Yeah.

83
00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:20.050
Or something.

84
00:03:20.270 --> 00:03:20.510
Something.

85
00:03:20.770 --> 00:03:22.630
Greg said, I agree.

86
00:03:23.070 --> 00:03:24.750
We can't lose any of this.

87
00:03:25.250 --> 00:03:27.210
Let's turn it into two episodes.

88
00:03:28.170 --> 00:03:29.830
And Ken said he was thrilled.

89
00:03:30.130 --> 00:03:30.850
That's amazing.

90
00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:32.410
That's how good it was.

91
00:03:32.410 --> 00:03:32.710
Yeah.

92
00:03:33.430 --> 00:03:36.610
Mindy and Ken turned in that good of an episode.

93
00:03:37.010 --> 00:03:43.670
Well, fast fact number two, when they broke up the episode into two episodes, they did

94
00:03:43.670 --> 00:03:47.470
actually need more storylines to fill out each half.

95
00:03:47.670 --> 00:03:52.770
So they knew that the lecture circuit story and the birthday party story would remain in

96
00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:56.850
both episodes, but it actually wasn't enough for two complete episodes.

97
00:03:56.930 --> 00:03:59.830
So they had to write two more stories.

98
00:04:00.070 --> 00:04:00.850
And what were those?

99
00:04:00.850 --> 00:04:07.570
I will tell you, for this episode, they added the storyline of Andy wanting to date Stanley's

100
00:04:07.570 --> 00:04:08.350
client, Julia.

101
00:04:09.050 --> 00:04:09.530
Yeah.

102
00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:12.770
That makes sense, because in the original script, it's not in there at all.

103
00:04:12.910 --> 00:04:13.070
No.

104
00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:18.670
And then for the second half, which we will get to next week, they wrote a very interesting

105
00:04:18.670 --> 00:04:20.730
storyline for you and your cats.

106
00:04:21.050 --> 00:04:21.830
Oh, yeah.

107
00:04:22.070 --> 00:04:23.470
I have stories, guys.

108
00:04:23.470 --> 00:04:30.610
So let's talk about this storyline with Stanley and his client, Julia, that they added.

109
00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:39.590
The reason that he doesn't meet with his client in the conference room is because the conference

110
00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:42.170
room was busy being a birthday party.

111
00:04:42.270 --> 00:04:42.590
Sure.

112
00:04:42.770 --> 00:04:43.690
It was being decorated.

113
00:04:43.910 --> 00:04:46.150
So they did all of that in the break room.

114
00:04:46.150 --> 00:04:51.750
And also, that way, they could insert it into the episode wherever they wanted, and it wouldn't

115
00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:54.050
affect any of the continuity of the other story.

116
00:04:54.050 --> 00:04:56.910
And they could shoot it later, because that's what we did.

117
00:04:57.370 --> 00:04:57.750
Yes.

118
00:04:58.070 --> 00:05:02.610
We shot these two additional storylines a full month later.

119
00:05:02.790 --> 00:05:03.130
Mm-hmm.

120
00:05:03.790 --> 00:05:05.090
That was the crazy thing.

121
00:05:05.230 --> 00:05:07.410
For me, they were like, okay, you have a whole storyline.

122
00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:08.690
It's going to be in lecture circuit.

123
00:05:08.890 --> 00:05:10.070
We're shooting it in three weeks.

124
00:05:10.250 --> 00:05:10.490
Yeah.

125
00:05:10.650 --> 00:05:10.790
What?

126
00:05:11.070 --> 00:05:12.270
Because they had to write it.

127
00:05:12.390 --> 00:05:12.570
Yeah.

128
00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:14.950
Should we move on to fast fact number three?

129
00:05:15.170 --> 00:05:16.250
Well, you sound eager.

130
00:05:16.390 --> 00:05:17.070
I think we should.

131
00:05:17.070 --> 00:05:19.050
Well, it's a location breakdown.

132
00:05:19.410 --> 00:05:20.990
You love a location breakdown.

133
00:05:21.310 --> 00:05:21.360
I really do.

134
00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:21.810
I know.

135
00:05:22.090 --> 00:05:25.390
I love knowing where we made this stuff happen.

136
00:05:25.530 --> 00:05:25.750
Yeah.

137
00:05:26.010 --> 00:05:27.930
You want to be in the room where it happens.

138
00:05:28.930 --> 00:05:29.490
Hamilton.

139
00:05:29.710 --> 00:05:30.010
Hey.

140
00:05:30.610 --> 00:05:32.110
Room where it happens.

141
00:05:32.390 --> 00:05:32.910
I love that.

142
00:05:33.050 --> 00:05:34.130
I really love that song.

143
00:05:34.190 --> 00:05:34.630
I do, too.

144
00:05:34.870 --> 00:05:35.150
Okay.

145
00:05:35.590 --> 00:05:38.150
We had a fan question from Joe S.

146
00:05:38.610 --> 00:05:45.390
Jenna, did you and Steve film your scenes in the car in a single day or multiple days?

147
00:05:45.390 --> 00:05:48.910
And where did you drive around to film the car scenes?

148
00:05:49.610 --> 00:05:50.450
I'll tell you.

149
00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:58.550
We shot all of the driving scenes for both Lecture Circuit 1 and Lecture Circuit Part 2 on the same one day.

150
00:05:58.770 --> 00:05:59.550
Oh, wow.

151
00:05:59.630 --> 00:06:01.070
So you had a full day in the car.

152
00:06:01.190 --> 00:06:01.370
Yep.

153
00:06:01.490 --> 00:06:02.210
Just driving around.

154
00:06:02.490 --> 00:06:02.890
Just driving around.

155
00:06:03.070 --> 00:06:04.990
It was Wednesday, November 5th.

156
00:06:05.150 --> 00:06:05.930
Look at you.

157
00:06:06.890 --> 00:06:10.130
Someone got the call sheet and looked at it.

158
00:06:10.210 --> 00:06:11.370
And that someone is Jenna Fisher.

159
00:06:11.610 --> 00:06:11.870
Yes.

160
00:06:11.990 --> 00:06:12.950
Thanks to James Carey.

161
00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:15.250
So here's where we went.

162
00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:18.450
We made a loop of three streets in North Hollywood.

163
00:06:20.310 --> 00:06:22.150
Nordhoff, Sadekoy, and Plummer.

164
00:06:22.350 --> 00:06:23.630
I recognize Sadekoy.

165
00:06:23.990 --> 00:06:24.330
Yeah.

166
00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:28.090
That's also the street that our sound stages were on.

167
00:06:28.170 --> 00:06:30.090
That's the street we drove on every single day.

168
00:06:30.250 --> 00:06:31.090
To get to work.

169
00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:31.350
Yeah.

170
00:06:31.970 --> 00:06:34.930
I will tell you, I was not actually driving in these scenes.

171
00:06:35.170 --> 00:06:35.930
You weren't?

172
00:06:36.030 --> 00:06:36.250
No.

173
00:06:36.390 --> 00:06:38.110
You did some good fakie driving.

174
00:06:38.110 --> 00:06:39.270
Thank you so much.

175
00:06:39.270 --> 00:06:41.390
I was going to ask you if you drove at all.

176
00:06:41.390 --> 00:06:42.030
I did not.

177
00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:42.350
Oh.

178
00:06:42.570 --> 00:06:46.750
They had the car loaded onto a rig and it was being pulled by a precision driver.

179
00:06:47.090 --> 00:06:47.350
Okay.

180
00:06:47.810 --> 00:06:49.710
I'm not much of a precision driver.

181
00:06:49.890 --> 00:06:52.250
I wouldn't describe myself that way at all.

182
00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:56.450
Precision is not the word I would think of to describe my driving.

183
00:06:57.430 --> 00:06:58.650
Jenna, I've ridden with you in a car.

184
00:06:58.830 --> 00:06:59.190
I know.

185
00:07:00.970 --> 00:07:03.070
So, you know, you're a very safe driver.

186
00:07:03.310 --> 00:07:03.630
Mm-hmm.

187
00:07:04.850 --> 00:07:06.210
But you, um.

188
00:07:08.630 --> 00:07:09.750
What are you going to say?

189
00:07:10.490 --> 00:07:11.630
You, I don't know.

190
00:07:11.710 --> 00:07:13.770
It's like you grip the wheel with both hands.

191
00:07:14.030 --> 00:07:14.310
I do.

192
00:07:14.430 --> 00:07:15.230
I'm a 10 and 2.

193
00:07:15.410 --> 00:07:16.450
You're a 10 and 2.

194
00:07:16.790 --> 00:07:19.830
And then you just kind of, you look straight ahead.

195
00:07:20.010 --> 00:07:22.830
And sometimes I'm like, you know, you can go around them, Jenna.

196
00:07:23.210 --> 00:07:25.810
There's a whole lane that's empty right next to you.

197
00:07:25.810 --> 00:07:29.270
We've been behind Pokey Pokerson for like half an hour.

198
00:07:29.830 --> 00:07:34.110
10 and 2, turn a little bit and go around them.

199
00:07:34.350 --> 00:07:35.870
Can I say something right now?

200
00:07:36.010 --> 00:07:36.250
Mm-hmm.

201
00:07:36.450 --> 00:07:38.990
This driving does actually sound very precise.

202
00:07:40.330 --> 00:07:40.930
Okay.

203
00:07:41.410 --> 00:07:42.030
Well, slow.

204
00:07:42.030 --> 00:07:45.030
Maybe I am a precision driver and I don't know it.

205
00:07:45.770 --> 00:07:49.330
You're a slow precision driver.

206
00:07:51.130 --> 00:07:55.910
You're not going to be taking any courses where you're like zipping around any cones.

207
00:07:55.910 --> 00:07:57.350
You'll get around those.

208
00:07:57.350 --> 00:08:00.390
Are you doing cone courses in your free time?

209
00:08:00.610 --> 00:08:00.830
Yeah.

210
00:08:01.050 --> 00:08:02.050
Is that your hobby?

211
00:08:02.050 --> 00:08:03.450
Do you not know this about me?

212
00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:05.790
I'm a freaking badass.

213
00:08:06.810 --> 00:08:07.730
Like, I do.

214
00:08:07.870 --> 00:08:11.070
I actually, by the way, I did pull off the road.

215
00:08:11.250 --> 00:08:13.130
Like, we did all that driving sequence.

216
00:08:13.130 --> 00:08:15.390
I was driving when Dwight runs me off the road.

217
00:08:15.650 --> 00:08:16.170
That was me.

218
00:08:16.870 --> 00:08:17.570
Oh, yeah.

219
00:08:17.570 --> 00:08:18.130
What do you want?

220
00:08:18.270 --> 00:08:18.930
What do you want?

221
00:08:19.010 --> 00:08:20.870
I want my precision driving trophy.

222
00:08:20.870 --> 00:08:23.850
It's a little gold, like, street cone.

223
00:08:24.490 --> 00:08:25.170
All right.

224
00:08:25.170 --> 00:08:27.790
I'll find one for you and I will get it for you.

225
00:08:28.130 --> 00:08:28.350
Okay.

226
00:08:28.690 --> 00:08:32.930
So, anyway, you were not driving, but you shot all in one day.

227
00:08:33.050 --> 00:08:34.150
We shot it all in one day.

228
00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:38.290
And then the next day, we shot everything at the Utica branch.

229
00:08:38.810 --> 00:08:42.250
And we started with all of the interior scenes.

230
00:08:42.770 --> 00:08:45.230
And we shot at this building in Chatsworth, California.

231
00:08:45.230 --> 00:08:46.970
It was on Hordoff Street.

232
00:08:47.190 --> 00:08:49.110
And we started very early that day.

233
00:08:49.210 --> 00:08:50.710
We started at 5.30 in the morning.

234
00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:52.010
That was your call time?

235
00:08:52.010 --> 00:08:52.750
Yeah.

236
00:08:52.990 --> 00:08:53.150
Yeah.

237
00:08:53.150 --> 00:08:57.570
And the crew call was 6.30 and the shooting call was 6.45.

238
00:08:58.010 --> 00:09:08.330
What that means is that we had the goal of arriving at 5.30, rehearsing at 6.30, and we had to start shooting by 6.45 a.m.

239
00:09:08.330 --> 00:09:09.330
That's an early day.

240
00:09:09.510 --> 00:09:10.290
And we did it.

241
00:09:10.970 --> 00:09:11.590
All right.

242
00:09:11.810 --> 00:09:18.310
So, before we go to break, lady, I think we should give a little book update.

243
00:09:18.750 --> 00:09:19.670
Book update?

244
00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:20.370
Office BFFs?

245
00:09:21.170 --> 00:09:24.790
Office BFFs is the name of our book that we have been working on for…

246
00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:25.690
Oh, good Lord.

247
00:09:25.850 --> 00:09:26.330
Three years.

248
00:09:26.530 --> 00:09:28.630
Longer than I can imagine.

249
00:09:28.930 --> 00:09:29.550
Oh, my goodness.

250
00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:33.470
We've been sharing on our Instagram, like, our journey as we're writing this together.

251
00:09:33.670 --> 00:09:34.510
And guess what?

252
00:09:34.610 --> 00:09:36.010
Well, you might know if you follow us.

253
00:09:36.090 --> 00:09:37.530
We finished our manuscript.

254
00:09:37.910 --> 00:09:39.230
We turned in our manuscript.

255
00:09:39.810 --> 00:09:41.270
Someone throw some confetti.

256
00:09:41.750 --> 00:09:42.230
Please.

257
00:09:42.590 --> 00:09:46.710
Your husband, Josh, did throw confetti when you told him that we had finished it.

258
00:09:46.830 --> 00:09:47.710
It was so sweet.

259
00:09:54.790 --> 00:09:55.810
So many photos.

260
00:09:56.110 --> 00:09:57.430
And they're so good.

261
00:09:57.550 --> 00:10:02.050
Because, you guys, the reason we wanted to write this book in the first place was because

262
00:10:02.050 --> 00:10:07.770
we did this big clean out of our garages and your shed and my basement.

263
00:10:08.030 --> 00:10:10.290
Basically, it's everywhere we stash stuff.

264
00:10:10.450 --> 00:10:10.670
Yeah.

265
00:10:10.770 --> 00:10:11.750
And you know what we found out?

266
00:10:12.070 --> 00:10:13.130
What did we find?

267
00:10:13.250 --> 00:10:14.230
We're big stashers.

268
00:10:15.090 --> 00:10:17.150
We did not need to find that out, lady.

269
00:10:17.170 --> 00:10:18.110
I think we knew that.

270
00:10:18.250 --> 00:10:18.930
Oh, my gosh.

271
00:10:19.230 --> 00:10:19.890
But it's true.

272
00:10:20.270 --> 00:10:22.510
And we saved everything.

273
00:10:22.510 --> 00:10:24.310
Every scrap of paper.

274
00:10:24.610 --> 00:10:25.390
Every ticket stub.

275
00:10:25.390 --> 00:10:25.950
Ticket stub.

276
00:10:26.170 --> 00:10:27.550
Here's the other thing, too.

277
00:10:27.730 --> 00:10:31.490
Not only do we save everything, but like our family does.

278
00:10:31.690 --> 00:10:37.170
I have a whole envelope from my cousin, Carol, of all of these clippings.

279
00:10:37.370 --> 00:10:38.010
Thank you, Carol.

280
00:10:38.470 --> 00:10:41.150
Well, all of this stuff is going in the book.

281
00:10:41.330 --> 00:10:43.310
I don't know that we can put all of it in the book.

282
00:10:43.390 --> 00:10:45.010
The book would be like 800 pages.

283
00:10:45.290 --> 00:10:45.950
That's true.

284
00:10:46.150 --> 00:10:49.290
Some of this stuff is going in the book, but it's all really fun.

285
00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:53.950
And you guys, I just am so excited for you to get it and to hold it in your hands and

286
00:10:53.950 --> 00:10:54.570
to have it.

287
00:10:54.730 --> 00:10:55.370
Me, too.

288
00:10:55.450 --> 00:10:57.570
I'm excited to go on our book tour.

289
00:10:58.330 --> 00:10:58.730
What?

290
00:10:59.670 --> 00:11:04.930
Lady, you know, when your book comes out, you go on a tour and you like sign it and

291
00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:05.850
you meet people.

292
00:11:06.090 --> 00:11:08.470
We're going to get to go on like a lady's...

293
00:11:08.470 --> 00:11:09.370
A road trip!

294
00:11:09.490 --> 00:11:10.090
A road trip!

295
00:11:10.110 --> 00:11:12.680
I am yelling.

296
00:11:12.840 --> 00:11:13.460
I'm so excited.

297
00:11:13.920 --> 00:11:18.980
Okay, you know this has been something I've wanted for a long time, which is a BFF road

298
00:11:18.980 --> 00:11:19.160
trip.

299
00:11:19.160 --> 00:11:20.020
I know, it's going to happen.

300
00:11:20.040 --> 00:11:22.740
Like a real deal road trip where we go to multiple cities.

301
00:11:23.040 --> 00:11:24.180
Well, it's happening.

302
00:11:24.500 --> 00:11:25.400
Get ready for it.

303
00:11:25.540 --> 00:11:29.720
Office BFFs with all our hoarded stuff and all of our great stories.

304
00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:31.760
It's coming your way soon.

305
00:11:31.840 --> 00:11:34.060
Oh my God, I didn't even think about going on tour.

306
00:11:34.720 --> 00:11:35.700
Well, there you go.

307
00:11:35.820 --> 00:11:36.920
There's our book update.

308
00:11:37.720 --> 00:11:38.600
Life update.

309
00:11:39.260 --> 00:11:40.780
Hit the road update!

310
00:11:40.780 --> 00:11:42.000
Look, I'm already excited.

311
00:11:42.100 --> 00:11:44.680
The book is not even done and I'm like planning our road trip.

312
00:11:45.280 --> 00:11:48.240
Oh, I have my places I like to stop and snack at.

313
00:11:49.360 --> 00:11:50.340
What are they?

314
00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:52.400
Where will I be snacking?

315
00:11:52.580 --> 00:11:56.300
I love a good, like, just greasy burger joint.

316
00:11:56.640 --> 00:11:57.240
For sure.

317
00:11:57.420 --> 00:11:57.640
Right?

318
00:11:57.840 --> 00:11:58.120
Mm-hmm.

319
00:11:58.280 --> 00:12:02.060
Also, I love the Frito Chili chips, you know?

320
00:12:02.960 --> 00:12:03.940
Oh, really?

321
00:12:03.940 --> 00:12:05.660
You're going to eat Frito Chili chips around me?

322
00:12:05.840 --> 00:12:07.600
Everyone says they stink up the room.

323
00:12:07.740 --> 00:12:08.360
It's so stinky, lady.

324
00:12:08.360 --> 00:12:08.760
I know.

325
00:12:08.860 --> 00:12:09.440
I love them.

326
00:12:09.720 --> 00:12:10.120
Okay.

327
00:12:10.460 --> 00:12:12.260
They're one of my go-to road trip snacks.

328
00:12:12.860 --> 00:12:13.380
Okay.

329
00:12:13.640 --> 00:12:14.000
Okay.

330
00:12:14.540 --> 00:12:15.060
All right.

331
00:12:15.160 --> 00:12:19.040
We're going to go to break now and I'm going to just try to convince Angela to eat regular Fritos.

332
00:12:19.340 --> 00:12:20.660
I love a regular Frito.

333
00:12:20.860 --> 00:12:22.280
Oh, especially with some queso.

334
00:12:22.600 --> 00:12:24.740
Oh, you know what I love a regular Frito with?

335
00:12:24.860 --> 00:12:25.100
What?

336
00:12:25.240 --> 00:12:26.240
A Frito Chili pie.

337
00:12:26.820 --> 00:12:27.920
I'm so hungry now.

338
00:12:27.920 --> 00:12:28.460
Like in the bag.

339
00:12:28.740 --> 00:12:29.140
I know.

340
00:12:29.340 --> 00:12:30.060
Give it to me.

341
00:12:30.080 --> 00:12:30.820
All right, we'll be back in a second.

342
00:12:31.340 --> 00:12:42.750
We are back.

343
00:12:42.750 --> 00:12:44.010
We're in this episode now.

344
00:12:44.250 --> 00:12:45.450
Michael, you guys.

345
00:12:45.850 --> 00:12:46.930
Oh my gosh.

346
00:12:47.110 --> 00:12:50.730
A phone guy came in to fix his phone and showed him the PA system.

347
00:12:50.730 --> 00:12:53.670
You can't show Michael Scott the office PA system.

348
00:12:53.910 --> 00:12:55.650
You definitely cannot.

349
00:12:56.050 --> 00:12:57.670
He is really goofing about now.

350
00:12:57.850 --> 00:12:58.090
Yeah.

351
00:12:58.090 --> 00:13:00.150
He pretends to be a plane captain.

352
00:13:00.330 --> 00:13:01.190
A ghoSt.

353
00:13:01.450 --> 00:13:01.610
Mm-hmm.

354
00:13:01.730 --> 00:13:05.530
He forgets the intercom is on while he's talking to his doctor about his mole.

355
00:13:05.750 --> 00:13:06.070
Blah.

356
00:13:06.250 --> 00:13:09.630
He calls Toby into the principal's office for wetting his bed.

357
00:13:11.570 --> 00:13:13.150
I think we should hear it.

358
00:13:13.290 --> 00:13:14.230
Can you play the clip?

359
00:13:14.490 --> 00:13:14.630
Yeah.

360
00:13:15.490 --> 00:13:16.830
Is your captain speaking?

361
00:13:54.040 --> 00:13:54.400
Ugh.

362
00:14:07.280 --> 00:14:09.420
My personal favorite part of that is the coughing.

363
00:14:09.420 --> 00:14:10.280
Yes.

364
00:14:10.580 --> 00:14:12.380
I loved listening to him cough.

365
00:14:12.660 --> 00:14:17.100
It reminded me of the tiramisu coughing fit that he had on the phone with David Wallen.

366
00:14:17.740 --> 00:14:22.020
Steve Krill is a master at fake laughing and fake coughing.

367
00:14:22.260 --> 00:14:22.420
Yeah.

368
00:14:23.020 --> 00:14:24.020
You believe it.

369
00:14:24.220 --> 00:14:26.460
We had a fan question from Virginia S.

370
00:14:26.600 --> 00:14:31.760
When Michael is on the PA system, were any of his announcements improvised or were they all in the script?

371
00:14:32.000 --> 00:14:36.720
For example, the announcement that Toby has wet his bed is hilarious.

372
00:14:37.500 --> 00:14:38.120
All right.

373
00:14:38.120 --> 00:14:39.620
They had several alts.

374
00:14:39.780 --> 00:14:44.320
And the one that was actually in the script for Toby read like this.

375
00:14:44.820 --> 00:14:49.800
Toby Flenderson to the principal's office, you are in trouble for sucking.

376
00:14:50.420 --> 00:14:51.560
That's pretty good.

377
00:14:51.560 --> 00:14:52.800
That's what was in the script.

378
00:14:53.380 --> 00:15:03.800
Well, I read the script while I watched this portion, and I would say that a lot of it was scripted, but Steve definitely did do improvisations off of what was written.

379
00:15:04.040 --> 00:15:06.800
And I'm sure Mindy was pitching things to him, too, on the day.

380
00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:14.500
Yes, but I noticed that the line about Ghost of Christmas Past, that was scripted, but the coughing bit was not in the script.

381
00:15:15.340 --> 00:15:20.740
Really quickly, I feel like we need to point out something at 27 seconds.

382
00:15:21.060 --> 00:15:21.700
What's that?

383
00:15:22.260 --> 00:15:23.940
What's up with Angela's outfit?

384
00:15:24.300 --> 00:15:25.140
What is it?

385
00:15:25.200 --> 00:15:28.760
It is a poofy, floofy sweater.

386
00:15:29.140 --> 00:15:29.700
Oh, yeah.

387
00:15:30.120 --> 00:15:32.640
But it's like poofy, like at the shoulder.

388
00:15:33.020 --> 00:15:35.780
That was really in, and I feel like that's coming back.

389
00:15:35.980 --> 00:15:36.260
What?

390
00:15:36.260 --> 00:15:37.720
Like the poofy arMs.

391
00:15:38.020 --> 00:15:38.380
Oh.

392
00:15:38.640 --> 00:15:43.000
We went through a real Shakespeare Renaissance fair thing back then.

393
00:15:43.160 --> 00:15:44.260
I'm not here for it.

394
00:15:44.520 --> 00:15:45.920
It's coming back, lady.

395
00:15:46.180 --> 00:15:46.540
Great.

396
00:15:46.860 --> 00:15:48.360
You know what I found in my closet?

397
00:15:48.680 --> 00:15:50.180
How do I describe this?

398
00:15:50.520 --> 00:15:53.700
I found a ribbon on a hanger.

399
00:15:53.920 --> 00:15:54.280
Okay.

400
00:15:54.500 --> 00:16:03.100
And then clipped to the ribbon were various flowers that I could put in my hair or on my lapel.

401
00:16:03.220 --> 00:16:04.940
You could adorn your outfit.

402
00:16:04.940 --> 00:16:10.400
Like one of the flowers was like a fabric flower that you would clip on your blazer.

403
00:16:10.640 --> 00:16:11.200
Oh, yeah.

404
00:16:11.740 --> 00:16:13.100
Was that in for a while?

405
00:16:13.180 --> 00:16:17.460
Why do I have seven flowers to clip to myself?

406
00:16:17.760 --> 00:16:18.400
I don't know.

407
00:16:18.500 --> 00:16:25.340
It feels very much like a pretty and pink, kind of like a Molly Ringwald with a flower on her hat.

408
00:16:25.540 --> 00:16:28.980
Yeah, it brought back no memories when I looked at it.

409
00:16:29.280 --> 00:16:31.560
Two of the flowers were like Hawaiian flowers.

410
00:16:31.560 --> 00:16:35.340
I clearly bought them to clip in my hair while on a trip to Hawaii.

411
00:16:35.600 --> 00:16:40.120
But the rest were more casual, more everyday.

412
00:16:40.160 --> 00:16:45.820
But I'm going to clip one on my blazer lapel when we do our book tour.

413
00:16:46.260 --> 00:16:47.020
All right?

414
00:16:47.100 --> 00:16:48.620
I'm planting that seed now.

415
00:16:48.760 --> 00:16:49.580
I can't wait.

416
00:16:49.580 --> 00:16:51.020
It's going to make me real happy.

417
00:16:51.020 --> 00:16:56.420
What I won't have on our book tour is a poofy sleeve sweater because at my age, I don't need

418
00:16:56.420 --> 00:16:57.540
any extra poofs.

419
00:16:57.700 --> 00:16:58.280
You know what?

420
00:16:58.340 --> 00:17:00.540
I'm going to say you will wear that on our book tour.

421
00:17:00.560 --> 00:17:00.880
No!

422
00:17:01.220 --> 00:17:02.320
Don't say that!

423
00:17:02.480 --> 00:17:06.140
Poofy sweater thing and flower lapel.

424
00:17:06.280 --> 00:17:07.840
Who are we on this book tour?

425
00:17:08.140 --> 00:17:08.840
I don't know.

426
00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:10.260
We're interesting people.

427
00:17:10.640 --> 00:17:12.300
Well, we'll see.

428
00:17:12.440 --> 00:17:14.600
Not dressed well, but interesting.

429
00:17:15.480 --> 00:17:16.200
All right.

430
00:17:16.620 --> 00:17:17.780
Let's get started.

431
00:17:18.480 --> 00:17:23.220
This episode opens with Michael exiting a motel room.

432
00:17:23.800 --> 00:17:26.780
He knocks on the neighboring door and out comes Pam.

433
00:17:27.220 --> 00:17:27.680
Yes.

434
00:17:27.820 --> 00:17:31.240
And in the shooting draft of our script, it says Michael knocks on Pam's door.

435
00:17:31.740 --> 00:17:33.140
They say good morning.

436
00:17:33.640 --> 00:17:34.280
That's it.

437
00:17:34.500 --> 00:17:36.780
They don't even have dialogue written out for you guys.

438
00:17:36.920 --> 00:17:38.220
You just sort of greet each other.

439
00:17:38.540 --> 00:17:40.160
This is not in the script.

440
00:17:40.160 --> 00:17:42.200
When Michael knocks, says hello, good morning.

441
00:17:42.360 --> 00:17:43.200
Pam says good morning.

442
00:17:43.200 --> 00:17:44.560
And then Michael says, you ready?

443
00:17:44.760 --> 00:17:46.900
And we're off like a herd of turtles.

444
00:17:47.360 --> 00:17:49.000
That is not in the script.

445
00:17:49.880 --> 00:17:51.660
I think Steve improvised that.

446
00:17:51.860 --> 00:17:57.120
I will tell you, I absolutely loved doing this episode because I got Steve all to myself.

447
00:17:57.300 --> 00:17:57.860
I bet.

448
00:17:58.120 --> 00:18:00.580
Just scene after scene of me and Steve.

449
00:18:00.800 --> 00:18:01.660
And I loved it.

450
00:18:01.960 --> 00:18:05.720
Some of my favorite times in the office were when I just got to have days with Steve,

451
00:18:06.240 --> 00:18:07.080
me and Steve.

452
00:18:07.400 --> 00:18:08.020
I know.

453
00:18:08.180 --> 00:18:11.920
They were brief and few and far between because, you know, Angela Martin hated him.

454
00:18:13.200 --> 00:18:14.100
They were always such a delight.

455
00:18:14.540 --> 00:18:18.640
Well, I love this scene of me putting the luggage into the back of the car.

456
00:18:19.300 --> 00:18:20.060
I did too.

457
00:18:20.220 --> 00:18:20.680
I'm sorry.

458
00:18:20.820 --> 00:18:21.520
I thought I did.

459
00:18:21.760 --> 00:18:22.940
I'm going to toot my own horn.

460
00:18:23.120 --> 00:18:25.980
I thought my heavy luggage acting was superb.

461
00:18:26.220 --> 00:18:28.740
It was so great that I wrote a question for you.

462
00:18:28.880 --> 00:18:30.220
Here's my fan question.

463
00:18:30.380 --> 00:18:30.640
Okay.

464
00:18:30.900 --> 00:18:31.740
What was in the bag?

465
00:18:31.740 --> 00:18:32.760
It looked really heavy.

466
00:18:33.040 --> 00:18:34.720
There was almost nothing in that bag.

467
00:18:34.920 --> 00:18:36.340
That was all me.

468
00:18:37.800 --> 00:18:38.540
Thank you.

469
00:18:39.140 --> 00:18:41.300
I mean, I couldn't be prouder of that.

470
00:18:41.480 --> 00:18:41.940
You know what?

471
00:18:42.040 --> 00:18:44.960
I won a Cone Award for my precision driving.

472
00:18:45.300 --> 00:18:47.560
I'm going to get you a little tiny suitcase.

473
00:18:47.780 --> 00:18:48.300
Thank you.

474
00:18:48.540 --> 00:18:50.500
That says great prop work.

475
00:18:50.720 --> 00:18:52.000
Prop work award.

476
00:18:52.560 --> 00:18:56.860
I don't know if you noticed, but we got a lot of mail about this car.

477
00:18:57.560 --> 00:19:01.780
Adele M wrote in and said, whose maroon Ford is Pam driving?

478
00:19:01.780 --> 00:19:06.100
I thought she had a Yaris and Michael had a PT Cruiser.

479
00:19:06.260 --> 00:19:07.040
What is this car?

480
00:19:07.920 --> 00:19:09.260
Is it a rental car?

481
00:19:09.780 --> 00:19:11.160
Listen to this.

482
00:19:11.360 --> 00:19:11.480
What?

483
00:19:11.560 --> 00:19:13.700
This is a gem from Randy Cordray.

484
00:19:14.240 --> 00:19:20.120
He said in an early concept meeting for this episode, it was discussed that Michael would

485
00:19:20.120 --> 00:19:26.040
need extra trunk space for all of his props and his trunk and all that stuff, and that

486
00:19:26.040 --> 00:19:28.000
it just wouldn't fit in his PT Cruiser.

487
00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:33.520
So they said that they thought it would be funny if Michael had to ask the company to

488
00:19:33.520 --> 00:19:40.640
provide him with a Lincoln Town car that Pam would drive him around in, but corporate would

489
00:19:40.640 --> 00:19:43.680
only approve a cheaper Crown Victoria.

490
00:19:44.440 --> 00:19:50.500
So this was always intended to be like a scripted moment where we would explain this, but in the

491
00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:52.260
end, it never made the shooting draft.

492
00:19:52.300 --> 00:19:55.900
So it comes off a bit confusing, but this was like a whole joke.

493
00:19:55.900 --> 00:19:59.240
I love it because Michael thinks he's Carrot Top, right?

494
00:19:59.460 --> 00:20:05.120
So he's got to have all of his props and his trunks of crazy gadgets and things.

495
00:20:05.360 --> 00:20:07.420
I mean, I'm surprised he didn't dress in a costume.

496
00:20:07.960 --> 00:20:15.020
I was too, but yet he gives Pam like some sass about her outfit and says, don't you know

497
00:20:15.020 --> 00:20:17.320
what a magician's assistant looks like?

498
00:20:17.740 --> 00:20:20.240
I Googled magician's assistant costume.

499
00:20:21.320 --> 00:20:22.500
There's a lot of fishnet.

500
00:20:22.780 --> 00:20:24.120
There's some short shorts.

501
00:20:24.360 --> 00:20:25.420
There's a bustier.

502
00:20:25.780 --> 00:20:26.820
There's a top hat.

503
00:20:27.100 --> 00:20:27.240
Yeah.

504
00:20:27.460 --> 00:20:28.240
Sometimes a skirt.

505
00:20:28.620 --> 00:20:30.160
It's a very sexy looking outfit.

506
00:20:30.580 --> 00:20:30.760
Yeah.

507
00:20:31.240 --> 00:20:34.220
Well, Pam wore her tan cardigan.

508
00:20:34.440 --> 00:20:35.160
It's new.

509
00:20:38.060 --> 00:20:43.140
I had such a hard time getting through that line because, of course, we knew that line

510
00:20:43.140 --> 00:20:44.060
was going to be in the script.

511
00:20:44.060 --> 00:20:49.140
So when we picked my outfit for this episode, we thought it was very funny that her new cardigan

512
00:20:49.140 --> 00:20:50.160
was like...

513
00:20:50.160 --> 00:20:50.760
Beige.

514
00:20:50.860 --> 00:20:51.400
Was beige.

515
00:20:53.480 --> 00:20:57.920
I have another amazing tidbit about this car before we get on the road.

516
00:20:58.220 --> 00:20:59.100
The toboggan?

517
00:20:59.340 --> 00:20:59.620
Yeah.

518
00:20:59.820 --> 00:21:00.840
That's on top of the car?

519
00:21:01.120 --> 00:21:01.700
All right.

520
00:21:02.160 --> 00:21:08.000
The reason that's there is because there was a scene that was written as a tag for this

521
00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:14.840
episode, and the scene was going to be Michael and Pam going down a snowy hill on that toboggan.

522
00:21:14.880 --> 00:21:16.540
Why didn't that happen?

523
00:21:19.240 --> 00:21:19.820
Yes.

524
00:21:20.320 --> 00:21:22.520
Well, we'd have to go somewhere with snow.

525
00:21:23.820 --> 00:21:30.520
Randy said they went out to scout a snowy mountain, and the photos that they came back

526
00:21:30.520 --> 00:21:32.240
with, it just didn't look great.

527
00:21:32.440 --> 00:21:36.600
There just wasn't a lot of snow happening at the time that we were shooting this episode.

528
00:21:36.600 --> 00:21:40.800
We couldn't go all the way to Mammoth, which is five hours away, right?

529
00:21:40.920 --> 00:21:47.300
We had to find some place that was relatively close, and there just was no snow, so we never

530
00:21:47.300 --> 00:21:47.860
