1568
01:03:06.040 --> 01:03:09.200
Well, it was played by writer Dan Gore.

1569
01:03:09.560 --> 01:03:09.940
Yeah.

1570
01:03:10.400 --> 01:03:12.880
He was a writer on Parks and Recreation.

1571
01:03:12.880 --> 01:03:17.240
Yes, and he had been working with Mike Schur and Greg Daniels as they developed that show.

1572
01:03:17.420 --> 01:03:21.460
And we had seen him a few times on set and in the writer's room meeting with those guys.

1573
01:03:21.960 --> 01:03:25.900
And he came to set one day when we were shooting on the stages,

1574
01:03:25.900 --> 01:03:28.420
and he and Rashida dressed up in all these different outfits,

1575
01:03:28.420 --> 01:03:30.300
and they went around and took pictures.

1576
01:03:32.380 --> 01:03:33.460
It was amazing.

1577
01:03:33.600 --> 01:03:34.220
It was amazing.

1578
01:03:34.560 --> 01:03:38.440
Well, you know, now Karen is going to ask about Jim.

1579
01:03:39.120 --> 01:03:39.560
Yes.

1580
01:03:39.560 --> 01:03:44.280
It's a little bit of tension, but Pam says we're engaged.

1581
01:03:44.560 --> 01:03:47.800
And Karen is just earnestly happy for them.

1582
01:03:48.080 --> 01:03:48.260
Yeah.

1583
01:03:48.720 --> 01:03:50.000
Rashida really sold it.

1584
01:03:50.120 --> 01:03:52.440
Because I think as an audience, you're like, oh, what's that?

1585
01:03:52.520 --> 01:03:55.180
And she's like, she has so moved on.

1586
01:03:55.340 --> 01:03:56.480
She has a whole life.

1587
01:03:56.540 --> 01:03:57.580
She's happy.

1588
01:03:57.580 --> 01:04:00.160
And it gives Pam closure.

1589
01:04:00.620 --> 01:04:01.040
Yeah.

1590
01:04:01.840 --> 01:04:09.260
I don't know about you, Ange, but I am happy if someone I have broken up with

1591
01:04:09.920 --> 01:04:14.640
finds, like, a new relationship with someone else and they're in love.

1592
01:04:15.200 --> 01:04:17.620
Because I'm like, yeah, that's why we broke up.

1593
01:04:17.680 --> 01:04:20.600
Because we weren't a match, and then you found your match.

1594
01:04:20.720 --> 01:04:23.180
I don't have a lot of hard feelings about stuff.

1595
01:04:23.320 --> 01:04:26.080
And I've had some messy breakups, you know?

1596
01:04:26.080 --> 01:04:28.200
And even still, I don't know.

1597
01:04:28.380 --> 01:04:30.780
I just, I think I am more Karen on this one.

1598
01:04:30.860 --> 01:04:31.620
I'm like, well, great.

1599
01:04:31.660 --> 01:04:35.220
I'm glad that worked out because, you know, good.

1600
01:04:35.460 --> 01:04:35.820
Mm-hmm.

1601
01:04:36.100 --> 01:04:40.120
It wasn't meant to be for me and Jim, but it's for you and Jim.

1602
01:04:40.280 --> 01:04:40.560
Right.

1603
01:04:41.240 --> 01:04:42.960
No, I think life is short.

1604
01:04:43.160 --> 01:04:45.940
My grandmother used to always say, every pot has its lid.

1605
01:04:46.140 --> 01:04:46.520
Mm-hmm.

1606
01:04:46.680 --> 01:04:48.520
And I want everyone to find their lid.

1607
01:04:48.840 --> 01:04:49.180
Yeah.

1608
01:04:49.520 --> 01:04:50.700
I wasn't your lid.

1609
01:04:50.800 --> 01:04:51.680
I fell in the water.

1610
01:04:51.800 --> 01:04:51.860
Yeah.

1611
01:04:52.340 --> 01:04:53.400
Or I was too big.

1612
01:04:53.680 --> 01:04:54.960
I was too big for your pot.

1613
01:04:54.960 --> 01:04:55.520
Yeah.

1614
01:04:55.980 --> 01:04:57.000
Or too small for your pot.

1615
01:04:57.560 --> 01:04:58.780
I didn't fit your pot.

1616
01:04:59.120 --> 01:05:00.400
Let's break it down some more.

1617
01:05:01.900 --> 01:05:04.560
I'm trying to see if there's a that's what she said in there.

1618
01:05:05.400 --> 01:05:06.740
But I can't find it.

1619
01:05:06.800 --> 01:05:08.240
My lid fit your pot perfect?

1620
01:05:08.840 --> 01:05:09.520
Mm-hmm.

1621
01:05:09.680 --> 01:05:09.920
No.

1622
01:05:10.380 --> 01:05:13.720
I think it would be, your pot fit my lid just right.

1623
01:05:14.420 --> 01:05:15.240
That's what she said.

1624
01:05:15.240 --> 01:05:16.780
I don't think either of them are real strong.

1625
01:05:16.780 --> 01:05:17.700
That's what she said.

1626
01:05:17.980 --> 01:05:19.040
We should let it go.

1627
01:05:19.600 --> 01:05:20.580
No, let's stick with it.

1628
01:05:20.580 --> 01:05:21.200
No, let's try it.

1629
01:05:21.260 --> 01:05:22.140
Let's try a few more.

1630
01:05:22.140 --> 01:05:23.340
Let's try a few more.

1631
01:05:24.280 --> 01:05:25.300
We'll find it.

1632
01:05:25.480 --> 01:05:26.380
We'll find it.

1633
01:05:27.320 --> 01:05:27.760
Everyone.

1634
01:05:28.040 --> 01:05:30.060
If you find it, will you email us?

1635
01:05:30.560 --> 01:05:31.180
Oh, no.

1636
01:05:31.180 --> 01:05:31.900
I didn't read this again.

1637
01:05:31.900 --> 01:05:33.140
What are you asking for?

1638
01:05:33.140 --> 01:05:33.740
I don't know.

1639
01:05:33.940 --> 01:05:34.220
All right.

1640
01:05:34.300 --> 01:05:35.660
Some interesting mail to read.

1641
01:05:35.780 --> 01:05:36.260
That's for sure.

1642
01:05:36.280 --> 01:05:36.860
That's for sure.

1643
01:05:37.600 --> 01:05:39.000
I don't know where we are.

1644
01:05:39.120 --> 01:05:40.040
We've hopped around.

1645
01:05:40.240 --> 01:05:41.180
Well, I'll tell you.

1646
01:05:41.300 --> 01:05:41.580
Okay.

1647
01:05:42.120 --> 01:05:44.580
Michael and Pam are going to leave the Utica branch.

1648
01:05:44.880 --> 01:05:45.260
All right.

1649
01:05:45.540 --> 01:05:47.400
Michael gives his lecture a B+.

1650
01:05:47.400 --> 01:05:49.620
He says Karen is mean.

1651
01:05:50.480 --> 01:05:52.060
Pam says, I like her.

1652
01:05:52.840 --> 01:05:58.860
And then Pam says she's glad she came along and that seeing Karen gave her closure.

1653
01:05:59.580 --> 01:06:05.840
Well, that's going to come back because as they're driving away, Michael tells Pam, you

1654
01:06:05.840 --> 01:06:06.300
know what?

1655
01:06:06.300 --> 01:06:08.300
I never got closure with Holly.

1656
01:06:08.760 --> 01:06:13.180
She was the love of my life and I never got closure.

1657
01:06:13.820 --> 01:06:20.580
So, Pam says, I think we should blow off this lecture in Rochester and go to Nashua instead.

1658
01:06:22.340 --> 01:06:24.560
Michael says, let's do it.

1659
01:06:25.140 --> 01:06:27.400
Pam is like, yeah, screw them.

1660
01:06:27.580 --> 01:06:28.580
Let's do this.

1661
01:06:29.440 --> 01:06:32.920
All of a sudden, Michael just got, what do the kids call it, a write or die?

1662
01:06:33.200 --> 01:06:34.300
He's like, yeah.

1663
01:06:34.640 --> 01:06:34.900
Yeah.

1664
01:06:35.160 --> 01:06:36.780
And then we have to be continued.

1665
01:06:37.240 --> 01:06:37.620
Yeah.

1666
